     a(a.p)(1 - sin h) + p sin h + (a x p) cos h, which is Rodrigues with
     cos(theta) = sin(h) and sin(theta) = cos(h) — a true orthonormal
     rotation about the unit axis by theta = 90 degrees - h. Worth saying
